/docker notes.md
Purpose: Docker command reference for building, running, and managing project containers.

/docker-compose.shattered-archive-experimental.yml
Purpose: Experimental Docker Compose stack for Shattered Archive development/testing; also the ONLY place MUD_WRITE_ENABLED=true is set (mud-builder-server service, sharing C:/Projects/merc-mud/2.4/area with the separately-composed game). Phase 15 (2026-07-25, live-verified): mud-builder-server's service block gained a docker.sock bind mount (RW) plus two READ-ONLY host-repo mounts (/host-merc-mud, /host-shattered-archive — distinct from its own build-time /repo copy) and MUD_REBUILD_ENABLED/MUD_REBUILD_ALLOWED_USERNAMES env vars — this is a deliberate, large blast-radius increase (root-equivalent host access from this one container) accepted knowingly, see the Phase 15 plan's Constraints. Step 7 (same day) added MERC_MUD_REPO_PATH=/host-merc-mud and SHATTERED_ARCHIVE_REPO_PATH=/host-shattered-archive — without these, config.ts's mercMudRepoPath/shatteredArchiveRepoPath fields would default to the narrow MERC_MUD_PATH (/mud, area-only) instead of the full repo mounts, breaking the rebuild pipeline's ability to read docker-compose.yml/Dockerfiles. MUD_REBUILD_ENABLED stays "false" — the rebuild pipeline code is live and deployed but the feature itself is not yet turned on; flipping it on for a real end-to-end run is a separate, deliberately gated action. Phase F (2026-07-28, live-verified): added kingdom-tactics-server (port 51000, secrets/ volume mount for its Ed25519 key, a named `kingdom-tactics-data` volume — deliberately NOT a host bind-mount like auth-server's data/, since match-history/army-layout JSON is pure app data, never hand-edited; AUTH_SERVER_URL set to the internal alias, AUTH_SERVER_PUBLIC_URL to the real public edge — the browser-redirect-vs-server-to-server split mud-builder-server never needed since it has no browser-facing SSO route of its own) and kingdom-tactics-client (plain static nginx serve, no VITE_ build args — same "relative URLs, edge routes them" pattern as mud-builder-client, confirmed as the REAL working convention by checking game-client.Dockerfile: it declares no ARG/ENV for the VITE_GAME_API/VITE_GAME_SECURE build args its OWN compose block passes, so those are silently unused today — VITE_SITE_API, added 2026-07-31, is the one such arg that IS declared and does take effect). Both new services share ONE subdomain (kingdom-tactics.shatteredarchive.dev, added to the edge nginx's alias list) rather than a client/server pair of subdomains. Scrum Poker (2026-07-28): added scrum-poker-server (63000, `scrum-poker-data` named volume for rooms.json, SCRUM_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS/SCRUM_ROOM_TTL_MS stated explicitly at their config.ts defaults since they are the two knobs anyone will want) and scrum-poker-client (VITE_AD_CLIENT/VITE_AD_SLOT build args, both empty by default = no ad code in the bundle), on the same single-subdomain scrum-poker.shatteredarchive.dev pattern. Unlike every other service here it holds NO service key and never calls auth-server — accounts-free by design. Present in BOTH compose files, unlike mud-builder/kingdom-tactics. Soulsteel GA4 (2026-08-14): nginx service gained NGINX_CSP_SOULSTEEL_FILE (defaults to the strict profile here, matching the dev-safety reasoning already given for NGINX_CSP_SCRUM_FILE), and soulsteel-client's build args gained VITE_GA_ID (defaults empty, same policy reasoning as SCRUM_GA_ID). Unlike scrum-poker this app never gets an ad-permitting profile — see deploy/nginx/includes/security-headers-analytics.conf. Simulacrum (2026-08-16, live-verified): added the simulacrum-server service block (build: simulacrum-server.Dockerfile, ports 65000-65001 internal only, shares merc-mud's `sa-shared` network alongside a read-only single-file bind mount onto mud-builder-server's roles.json for the shared trusted+ tier check) plus `simulacrum.shatteredarchive.dev` in nginx's alias list and `simulacrum-server` in auth-server's SERVICE_REGISTRY env var. Corrected game-server's GAME_PROXY_ALLOWLIST from the wrong `simulacrum.shatteredarchive.dev:4000` to the real internal target `simulacrum-server.shatteredarchive.dev:65001` (merc-mud's raw port is never reachable directly). Removed a stale `extra_hosts: host-gateway` entry found unused during the same pass. Live bug fix (2026-08-16, found via a user report): `mud-builder-server` was missing from auth-server's `SERVICE_REGISTRY` entirely, silently revoking its registered key (a 3-week-old regression from when SERVICE_REGISTRY replaced the old manual register-service flow, not caused by this session's own earlier edits) and breaking every account-based sign-in against it. Added `"mud-builder-server": {"redirectUris": []}` (empty — no browser-redirect SSO flow, device-credential/pasted-key only) and re-ran the registration ceremony (recreate auth-server, register-service again, replace the mounted secret, restart mud-builder-server) since being un-pruned doesn't restore an already-revoked key by itself.

/docker-compose.yml
Purpose: This file orchestrates a production deployment of a web and game archive platform using Docker containers and nginx reverse proxy. Scrum Poker (2026-07-28): gained scrum-poker-server (63000, `scrum-poker-data` named volume for rooms.json) and scrum-poker-client — additive like auth, NOT in nginx's depends_on, and deliberately unconnected to auth-server (an accounts-free tool: the room id (a UUID) is membership, the create-time host token is organizer). Note this prod file still carries no kingdom-tactics service; that lives only in the experimental stack. Soulsteel GA4 (2026-08-14): nginx service gained NGINX_CSP_SOULSTEEL_FILE, defaulting to security-headers-analytics.conf (analytics ON by default here, mirroring NGINX_CSP_SCRUM_FILE/NGINX_CSP_LANDING_FILE's prod defaults) — never the ads profile, this app carries no ad unit. soulsteel-client's build args gained VITE_GA_ID, defaulting to the SAME GA4 property id as scrum-poker/landing (G-7BKPVVZ1BS); analytics.ts's per-hostname cookie_domain pin is what keeps the three from sharing a visitor identity despite the shared property. Same-day: auth-server's SERVICE_REGISTRY here was ALSO missing both simulacrum-server and mud-builder-server (the live bug found on the experimental stack — see the note on that compose file — applies here too, just never actually exercised since neither service is deployed to this prod file for real yet, mud-builder-server especially). Added both with a comment explaining a bare declaration with no published key is a harmless no-op per the reconciler's own design, so pre-declaring now avoids rediscovering this exact bug later. Simulacrum (2026-08-16): gained `simulacrum.shatteredarchive.dev` in nginx's alias list, `simulacrum-server.shatteredarchive.dev:65001` in game-server's GAME_PROXY_ALLOWLIST, and a full simulacrum-server service block mirroring soulsteel-server's prod shape — this one carries an explicit in-file comment flagging that mud-builder-server is NOT deployed to prod yet, so the shared-role-store bind-mount path is a best guess: simulacrum will be reachable but fails closed (no tier ever resolves above `user`) until that gap is resolved. mud-builder-server itself is still experimental-only, unlike simulacrum-server.

/game-client.Dockerfile
Purpose: This Dockerfile builds and deploys the game client application with Node.js and Nginx. Declares ARG/ENV only for VITE_PORT, VITE_WEB_API, VITE_WEB_WS, VITE_WEB_SECURE, VITE_ENV and VITE_SITE_API — the last added 2026-07-31 because apps/game-client/.env ships inside the build context naming this machine's dev values, so a build arg that is NOT redeclared here loses to that file (a real process env var is what overrides a .env entry in vite).

/game-server.Dockerfile
Purpose: This Dockerfile builds and runs the game server application in a production environment.

/index.html
Purpose: The shatteredarchive.dev landing page — a static, dependency-free, single-file hub. Served by the FRONT proxy from /var/www/shatteredarchive-dev, NOT through this repo's edge nginx, so no deploy/nginx/includes/security-headers*.conf reaches it; it declares its own policy via <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy"> which must stay in step with the real header on the apex block in DSL/nginx/shattered_archive.site (a browser enforces the INTERSECTION of the two). Rewritten 2026-08-05 from a pure "your hosts file is misconfigured" notice into a demo hub: sticky nav wrapper, a static demo-card grid (live cards are <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">; kingdom-tactics. is a non-clickable "Coming soon" <div> because it is still a 503 stub on the front proxy), the original self-hosting instructions, and ONE Google ad unit. Simulacrum (2026-08-16): MUD Builder flipped from `demo-soon` to a live `<a>` card (mentions free-to-browse, trusted+-to-edit), and a NEW Simulacrum live card was added right after it — framed as "sign in and request access" rather than "play now" (trusted+-only), and as a near-stock ROM 2.4 baseline, never compared to a specific real MUD by name. Same-day follow-up: the self-hosting section's "Map the development domains" `<ul>` was stale — it claimed to list everything `pnpm setup:hosts:win/nix` writes but was missing the apex plus `build.`/`kingdom-tactics.`/`soulsteel.` (pre-existing gaps) AND `simulacrum.` (new; the scripts themselves were ALSO missing it — see deploy/scripts/.annotated). Fixed the list here to match the corrected scripts exactly, and updated the "Bring the stack up" paragraph to mention Simulacrum needs the experimental stack specifically (its container ships in the default file too, but fails closed there without MUD Builder's shared role store). The same file is also served at `location = /` on game-server. and web-client., so edits surface on those roots too. Ad + GA4 config and init live in the EXTERNAL /site.js (see below), not inline — that move is what lets the CSP drop 'unsafe-inline' from script-src. The <style> block stays inline deliberately: style-src needs 'unsafe-inline' regardless (AdSense injects inline styles), style injection is not script execution, and externalising the CSS would break rendering under the game-server./web-client. roots, whose blocks proxy every non-`/` path to Docker.

/kingdom-tactics-client.Dockerfile
Purpose: Phase F — digest-pinned multi-stage build of the Kingdom Tactics client (vite build → nginx static), mirrors mud-builder-client.Dockerfile exactly: no VITE_KT_API/VITE_KT_WS build args, the client calls /api/kt and /ws/kt relatively (see features/auth/kt-auth-config.ts) and the edge nginx routes them on the SAME subdomain.

/kingdom-tactics-server.Dockerfile
Purpose: Phase F — digest-pinned multi-stage build of the Kingdom Tactics server (node alpine, pnpm via strict corepack, port 51000), modeled on game-server.Dockerfile (same bootstrap shape) rather than mud-builder-server.Dockerfile — includes the `COPY deploy/.env /repo/.env` step game-server has and mud-builder-server doesn't; a real deploy crash (missing /repo/.env) caught this omission on the first container start, not review. Also builds @shatteredarchive/kingdom-tactics-engine, which neither game-server nor mud-builder-server need.

/mud-builder-client.Dockerfile
Purpose: Digest-pinned multi-stage build of the MUD Builder UI (vite build → nginx static, no VITE_ args — the client calls /api relatively and the edge routes it).

/mud-builder-server.Dockerfile
Purpose: Digest-pinned multi-stage build of the MUD Builder API server (node alpine, pnpm via strict corepack, port 61000); write gate deliberately unset in the image. Phase 15: runtime stage installs docker-cli + docker-cli-compose (apk) right after the CVE-patch upgrade line — unused image capability until the compose file's docker.sock mount (see .annotated above) gives it something to talk to.

/nginx.Dockerfile
Purpose: Nginx Dockerfile configuring SSL, logging, and entrypoint for edge subdomains.

/privacy.html
Purpose: Privacy & cookies notice for the shatteredarchive.dev constellation (new 2026-08-05), served from the same docroot as index.html and linked from the nav, footer and scrum-poker's footer. Deliberately carries NO ads and NO analytics, which is why its meta CSP is genuinely strict (`script-src 'none'`, no third-party allowlist) — do not copy index.html's looser policy onto it. Documents the ad/analytics split (AdSense on the landing page and scrum-poker only; never the auth hub, never *.com), a full cookie/localStorage table incl. sa_session's host-only+HttpOnly scoping and scrum-poker's per-room credentials, per-service server-side retention (scrum-poker: 1h participant idle, 30d room TTL), and what the ad unit is prevented from doing (Privacy Sandbox APIs off). The .com-side policy stays in the repo root PRIVACY.md, which now scopes itself and points here. Soulsteel (2026-08-14): added as the doc's third analytics-only host (GA yes, AdSense no) — new row in the advertising/analytics table, an explicit mention in the Google Analytics section and the `_ga`/`_ga_*` cookie row, and a new "Soulsteel" subsection under server-side storage noting it has no accounts and no server-side game storage (state lives in the browser's IndexedDB; soulsteel-server never sees it) — first time this app is mentioned in the doc at all, since it previously had no privacy-doc presence. Simulacrum (2026-08-16): added to the build.+kingdom-tactics. ads/analytics table row (No/No, unchanged) and given its own "What each service stores on the server" subsection — the short-lived single-use access code, the account-ID-to-character link that surfaces on the Auth Hub dashboard, and the disposable-demo-world framing already established by the callout at the top of the page.

/scrum-poker-client.Dockerfile
Purpose: Digest-pinned multi-stage build of the Scrum Poker client (vite build → nginx static). Unlike mud-builder-client/kingdom-tactics-client it DOES declare build args — VITE_AD_CLIENT/VITE_AD_SLOT, and they are genuinely wired (ARG + ENV, read via Vite `define`), unlike game-client's declared-nowhere VITE_* args. Both default to empty, and with either empty nothing renders and the page makes no request to any ad network (the unreachable loader code does remain in the bundle — AdSlot's injectable config prop, which exists for testability, stops the minifier proving the branch dead; the guarantee is no ad REQUEST, not no ad code). Everything else (API + websocket) uses same-origin relative URLs the edge routes.

/scrum-poker-server.Dockerfile
Purpose: Digest-pinned multi-stage build of the Scrum Poker server (node alpine, pnpm via strict corepack, port 63000). Modeled on kingdom-tactics-server.Dockerfile including its `COPY deploy/.env /repo/.env` step; also builds @shatteredarchive/scrum-poker-core, the isomorphic package the client shares. No secrets mount and no service key — this service does not talk to auth-server.

/simulacrum-server.Dockerfile
Purpose: Digest-pinned multi-stage build of simulacrum-server (node alpine, pnpm via strict corepack) mirroring soulsteel-server.Dockerfile's shape — builds the Express+relay TS service, copies src/public (the standalone sign-in page) into dist/public since tsc alone won't carry static assets, ships a service key mount point at /repo/apps/simulacrum-server/secrets for the auth-server introspect fallback (same convention as mud-builder-server's).

/site.js
Purpose: Ad + GA4 initialisation for the shatteredarchive.dev landing page (new 2026-08-05), deployed to /var/www/shatteredarchive-dev alongside index.html and privacy.html. EXISTS AS A FILE for exactly one reason: so the page's CSP can say `script-src 'self' <google hosts>` with NO 'unsafe-inline'. That token does not create an XSS, it removes the mitigation that would neuter one, and the apex is the worst place in the domain to give it up — script running there can set a `Domain=.shatteredarchive.dev` cookie that every sibling subdomain receives. All-or-nothing contract mirroring scrum-poker's AdSlot.tsx: with AD_CONFIG.client/slot empty the container is removed from the DOM and no ad network is contacted; with GA_ID empty no gtag request is made and no cookie is set. GA pins cookie_domain to location.hostname so `_ga` is NOT scoped to the registrable domain and never reaches auth.shatteredarchive.dev. Requests `data-ad-format="rectangle"` + `full-width-responsive="false"` — overriding the console's responsive default on purpose — so the unit stays in the square/rectangle family inside a 336px container. A missing site.js yields a page with no ad and no analytics: fails safe, silently. This file 404s under the game-server./web-client. roots, which is fine and preferable.

/sitemap.xml
Purpose: Sitemap for the shatteredarchive.dev constellation (new 2026-08-05), deployed to /var/www/shatteredarchive-dev with the other docroot files and served via an exact-match `location = /sitemap.xml { try_files /sitemap.xml =404; }` in the front proxy — the =404 is load-bearing, because `location /` ends in `/index.html` and a missing file would otherwise return the landing page's HTML with a 200 under an .xml URL (Search Console reports that as an unparseable sitemap, a confusing way to learn the file was never deployed). THREE URLs only: the apex `/`, `/privacy`, and scrum-poker's root. That is not incomplete coverage — a sitemap may only list URLs a crawler is ALLOWED to fetch, and every other constellation host deliberately serves `Disallow: /`, so listing them would produce one "Submitted URL blocked by robots.txt" error each and index nothing. The apex page IS the constellation index: it names and describes every service in crawlable HTML. The scrum-poker entry is cross-host, authorised by that host's robots.txt naming this same sitemap in its `Sitemap:` directive (the sanctioned ownership signal); a DNS-verified Search Console domain property is the belt-and-braces version. Hand-maintained on purpose (three URLs, static docroot, no build step); the .com sitemap is the opposite case — hundreds of data-driven pages — and is generated from the C# app, see .ai-plans/20260805-1500-sitemaps-and-seo.md. Namespace must be sitemapS.org (plural) or the file is rejected outright as an unknown format.

/soulsteel-client.Dockerfile
Purpose: Digest-pinned multi-stage build of the Soulsteel client (vite build → nginx static). Previously had no build-time configuration at all (relative-URL API only, like mud-builder-client/kingdom-tactics-client). Gained VITE_GA_ID (2026-08-14), same all-or-nothing contract as scrum-poker-client.Dockerfile's — empty means no gtag script, no cookie, no request. Unlike scrum-poker there is no matching VITE_AD_* pair here and never will be; this app carries no ad unit.

